No upstream source: this rubygems RBS extras stub is hand-written
by Rigor maintainers under MPL-2.0 (matching the rest of Rigor).
The rbs gem ships partial `core/rubygems/*.rbs` coverage already
(loaded via Ruby core RBS, no opt-in needed), but the surface
omitted there — `Gem.target_rbconfig` / `Gem.verbose` /
`Gem.load_safe_marshal` / `Gem::Platform#initialize` /
`Gem::Dependency#initialize` / `Gem::Specification.find_all_by_name`
etc. — surfaces hundreds of false positives when rigor analyses
rubygems' or bundler's own source code.

This file is a SUPPLEMENT — it re-opens the upstream classes /
the Gem module to ADD the missing declarations only, never
redeclaring anything the upstream RBS already covers, so the
loader does not raise `RBS::DuplicatedDeclarationError`.

Modelled on `lib/rubygems/defaults.rb` and the survey at
`docs/CURRENT_WORK.md` § "Queued engine items".
